Description: Add U: host prefix to connect to a Unix-domain socket
 Adds a U: host prefix so that c3270, s3270, x3270, b3270 and tcl3270 can
 connect to a TN3270 server listening on a Unix-domain socket (e.g. QEMU's
 x-terminal3270 behind -chardev socket,path=...,tn3270=on), e.g.
 "c3270 U:/run/qemu-server/100.tn3270". Backport to 4.3ga10.
Author: Yvan Janssens <yvanj@cyber.gent>
Origin: other, https://github.com/cyberdotgent/x3270/commit/549eaefe844e9ae78638d230bf33b662aa6d5779
Forwarded: not-yet (prepared for https://github.com/pmattes/x3270, main-branch version: https://github.com/cyberdotgent/x3270/commit/4d0e0bb206caa030dd7fbac0d33fe34b509b325e)
Last-Update: 2026-11-18
